What is the name of this solid?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0.85); \coordinate (B) at (0.8,0); \coordinate (C) at (2,0.4); \coordinate (D) at (2,1.7); \coordinate (E) at (0.8,2.2);
\coordinate (F) at (1.2,1.55); \coordinate (G) at (2,0.7); \coordinate (H) at (3.2,1.1); \coordinate (I) at (3.2,2.4); \coordinate (J) at (2,2.9);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--(E)--cycle;
\draw (C)--(H)--(I)--(J)--(E); \draw (D)--(I);
\draw[dashed] (A)--(F)--(G)--(H); \draw[dashed] (B)--(G); \draw[dashed] (F)--(J);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This pyramid has a square base.
What is its name?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0); \coordinate (B) at (3,0); \coordinate (C) at (4,0.8); \coordinate (D) at (1,0.8); \coordinate (P) at (2,3.45);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C); \draw[dashed] (C)--(D)--(A);
\draw (P)--(A) (P)--(B) (P)--(C); \draw[dashed] (P)--(D);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
